    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illūsĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inl-</span></b> ), ōnis,
			f.
		illudo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mocking</i>, <i>jeering; irony</i>,
			a figure of speech, = derisio, insultatio, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 3, 53, 202</span></i>; also ap. <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				1, 28</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 8, 6, 54</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An illusion</i>, <i>deceit</i> (eccl.
			Lat.), <i><span class="en">Vulg. Psa. 37, 7</span></i>; Isa. 66, 4.</div>
